Below is a concise C program that implements the necessary check.  
It hinges on the key insight that for the distribution to be fair,  
in every suffix of the toys (from the right), the absolute difference  
between the number of toys given to Alice and Bob must not exceed 1.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(){
    int T;
    scanf("%d",&T);
    while(T--){
        int N;
        scanf("%d",&N);

        char S[N+1];
        scanf("%s", S);

        int count1 = 0, count0 = 0, fair = 1;

        // Check suffixes from right to left
        for(int i = N - 1; i >= 0; i--){
            if(S[i] == '1') count1++;
            else count0++;
            if(abs(count1 - count0) > 1){
                fair = 0;
                break;
            }
        }

        puts(fair ? "YES" : "NO");
    }
    return 0;
}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Explanation of the core idea:  
• For each input distribution string S, scan from the right.  
• Keep track of how many '1's (Alice's toys) and '0's (Bob's toys)  
  have been seen so far.  
• At any point, if these counts differ by more than 1, we can assign  
  sufficiently large values to those last toys to make the difference  
  exceed the largest toy’s value, violating the fairness condition.  
• Otherwise, if we never exceed this difference, the distribution is fair.

#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    int T;
    scanf("%d", &T);
    while(T--) {
        int N, X;
        scanf("%d %d", &N, &X);
        /*
          We have 2*N players in total, X of them are rated.
          We want to minimize the number of rated players facing rated opponents.
          - If X <= N, we can pair all rated with unrated, so the answer is 0.
          - Otherwise, leftover rated players are (X - (2*N - X)) = 2X - 2N.
            Each of these must face a rated opponent, so the answer is 2(X - N).
        */
        int result = (X <= N) ? 0 : 2 * (X - N);
        printf("%d\n", result);
    }
    return 0;
}

